Usage Guideline: CHIPS_PaymentReturn_pacs.004.001.10
Base Message: pacs.004.001.10
Date of publication: 14 March 2025
URL: https://www2.swift.com/mystandards/#/mp/mx/_0Xae0FsuEe-zxKLujiTfgQ/_0dJ6cFsuEe-zxKLujiTfgQ
Description: When this message is sent TO CHIPS:
The CHIPS_PaymentReturn message is sent by a CHIPS Participant to CHIPS in order to return a previously settled  pacs.008 or pacs.009 (including the pacs.009 cover). The pacs.004 must be used to return a previously settled CHIPS payment and may also be used to return a payment settled through another clearing mechanism. The pre-pended BAH/BusinessService element must contain TC10 (Transaction Code value for the Payment Message).  

When this is a Message sent FROM CHIPS: 
The CHIPS_PaymentReturn message is sent by CHIPS to the receiving CHIPS Participant. The pre-pended BAH/BusinessService element will contain RC31 (the Response Code value for the Receive Notification).

Payments received after the cutoff time will be rejected. 
 - pacs.002 RJCT
 - Error Code C0025
 - Additional Information Text: Past Cutoff
Generated by the MyStandards web platform [https://www.swift.com/mystandards] on 2025-03-27T07:59:48Z
The Clearing House Payments Company LLC notices : CHIPS went live with ISO 20022 for all its participant messaging on April 8, 2024. The next CHIPS release (to coincide with the Swift/CBPR+ SR2025 release) is scheduled for November 24, 2025. 
